2615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the search test investigation to a subagent while I look at the others.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nThe whole suite now passes: `python3 -m unittest` runs 16 tests with no failures. Before the fixes it ran 15 and reported 6 failures and 4 errors. The count went up because `test_search.py` couldn't be imported and counted as one error; now its two real tests run.\n\nI gave the `test_search.py` failure to a subagent to investigate. It found that the import was the only problem in that file, and I tracked the work with the todo list. I didn't change any tests.\n\nFixes in `catalog/`:\n- **`search.py`**: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports it from `catalog.text`.\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` now turns the year into an integer instead of leaving it as text. This also fixes `Book.age()`, which crashed trying to subtract text from a number.\n- **`factory.py`**: added the missing third sample book, `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`.\n- **`fees.py`**: the late fee is now days late \u00d7 the daily rate (`days_late * DAILY_FEE`); it was adding them instead.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns the last `n`. I also made it return an empty list when `n <= 0`, which no test requires.\n- **`members.py`**: raised `MAX_BORROWED` from 3 to 5, matching the comment above it and the tests.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 52626, 